                {'stem': 'The Amsler grid is a useful COMPLEMENT to macular OCT because it:', 'options': ['Lets the patient self-monitor between visits', 'Replaces the need for an OCT scan entirely', 'Measures the retinal thickness in microns', 'Produces a colour photograph of the retina'], 'correct': [0], 'qtype': 'single', 'kind': 'situational', 'explanation': 'The grid is a cheap, at-home subjective monitor; OCT gives objective structural detail in clinic - they work together.', 'reasoning_eligible': True},
