                {'stem': "For a patient with end-stage glaucoma whose HVF is 'too noisy' to interpret, GVF is offered. The value is that it:", 'options': ['Can still map the residual peripheral island', 'Cures the glaucoma while the field is being mapped', 'Measures the corneal thickness at the same time', 'Removes any need for further follow-up visits'], 'correct': [0], 'qtype': 'single', 'kind': 'situational', 'explanation': 'When central automated testing is unrewarding in end-stage disease, kinetic GVF maps the remaining peripheral field for monitoring.', 'reasoning_eligible': True},
